# The tutorial's window (TutWin, see tutwin.c): a note about the square of the first unit, asked for the way the game asks (the script
# host's "open tut_terrain" calls tut_map, which moves the map to the square and opens the note, a modal popup at the bottom left with
# an arrow from it to the square, and a Close button). The note is mode 0: one button, and the arrow to the square. The state
# regions are the window object's fields from tile_x (0x8cc1e4) on (the square, the arrow's ends, whether a note is up, what it is about,
# what answered it), the two flags at 0x8cc244, the tutorial's "shown" words at 0x9a64ac, the callback the popup draws its picture with
# (0x8c9fd0) and the popup's size (0x8c9f24).
25 load
26 state tw_fields 0x8cc1e4 0x5c
26 state tw_flags 0x8cc244 8
26 state tw_seen 0x9a64ac 0x14
26 state tw_draw 0x8c9fd0 4
26 state tw_size 0x8c9f24 8
44 open tut_terrain
50 snap open
52 move 324 736
56 snap hover
58 move 800 300
62 snap hover-out
64 click 324 736          # the Close button
68 snap closed
70 close
